  "limitations": [
    "Specific Kapaleeshwarar standing core: twelve mapped gateway/shrine/mandapa/perimeter-roof envelopes, tall seven-tier eastern gopuram and smaller western gopuram with true through-passages, granite bases and receding painted bands/central niches, curved crests/finials and original simplified sculptural vocabulary. Two inner shrine roof masses, real open pillared mandapas, red/white parapet rhythms, stone plinths and brass flagstaff. Courtyards, tank, streets and independent surrounding buildings stay host context. No copied deity/narrative/text atlas or complete ritual interior.",
    "Named standard PMTiles temple-complex point35185920244763 correlates the twelve core building envelopes with the ordinary gateway/courtyard pictures; no exact-QID building-footprint match is claimed. Anchor80.26972222,13.03388889; heading0, internal local+x angle+.245rad. Eastern gateway at local[62.5,23.9], western gateway[-16.4,18.2]; both passages run approximately east/west. Main core halls/shrines follow mapped envelopes; facade/roof/sanctum splits and fine stations are picture/map-led approximations. Preserve the separate southeastern building35184580656517.",
    "Picture-led eastern tower about37m including6m granite base, seven receding painted storeys and curved crest/finials; western tower about16m with three levels. Pillared halls about4.6m, main inner shrine about13m and secondary shrine about12m including simplified painted roof masses. Tower footprints, roof envelopes and spacing use standard map controls. Storey heights, sculptural inventory, shrine caps, column grid, facade/roof splits and exact parapet rhythm are approximate.",
    "Retain original standard6m Mapzen urban ground/water and all independent buildings. Each mapped range uses a local level floor and constant buried plinth bottom sampled along boundary edges. Court remains open native ground; short gateway thresholds/approaches connect to local grade. No broad courtyard slab, terrain flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse urban DEM does not resolve exact paved thresholds, temple plinth levels or tank embankments; elevations remain approximate.",
